// D4346 — a CALL through a value narrowed to the function arm of a value union
// (`((x: i32) => i32) | string`). The `*_place` positions are the ingredient: the place
// (`h.f`, `xs[0]`, `m[k]`) is the callee, and a narrowed place was not classified as a
// closure, so the call had no lowering. A bare binding always ran.
//
// The PROOF discriminates: it calls the narrowed value, so a fold of the test to a constant
// prints `9`, and a wrong closure prints anything but `8`.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function mk(n: i32): ((x: i32) => i32) | string {
  if n == 0 { return "s" }
  return (x: i32) => x + n
}
// @@VALUE@@
mk(1)
// @@TYPE@@
((x: i32) => i32) | string
// @@FALLBACK@@
mk(2)
// @@TEST@@
v is (x: i32) => i32
// @@HIT@@
print(v(7))
// @@MISS@@
print(9)
// @@WANT@@
8
